# Connecting FLU UGVs to the {{ site.customer or site.name }} server

These files are for your server administrator. The UGVs connect to your
WireGuard server themselves and keep the tunnel up (keepalive 25 s); no
inbound connections to the UGVs are needed.

## What to configure on your server

1. A WireGuard server on `{{ site.endpoint }}` (UDP), server public key:
   `{{ site.server_pubkey }}`
2. Server address in the tunnel: `{{ server_ip }}` in `{{ site.network.tunnel }}`.
3. Add the peers from `peers.conf` (one per UGV).
4. Routes to the UGV networks (`{{ site.network.robot_lans }}`) must go through the WireGuard interface.
   `wg-quick` does this automatically from AllowedIPs.
5. Tunnel MTU {{ mtu }} (LTE MTU is smaller than the standard one).

A UGV accepts MAVLink and camera connections only from:
{% for src in site.sources() %}
`{{ src }}`{{ "," if not loop.last else "." }}
{% endfor %}
If you need to connect from other addresses, tell us and we will update the UGVs.

